  "body": "Hanene Street, St Heliers – Auckland’s Most Prestigious Address\r\nDiscover the Residence: www.3and5hanene.com\r\n\r\nIf you’ve been searching for a once-in-a-generation new home on one of Auckland’s most prestigious clifftop streets—with breathtaking 270° harbour views and architectural brilliance beyond compare—this is the property for you.\r\n\r\nCommanding a prized double block atop the glittering Waitemata Harbour, this brand-new, world-class residence is a showcase of design excellence and uncompromising luxury. With its perfect north-facing aspect and sweeping views from Rangitoto Island to the Harbour Bridge, this is a home that will take your breath away—and never give it back.\r\n\r\nSet across four exquisite levels on an expansive 1,613 m² freehold estate, every inch of this home has been meticulously crafted for those who demand the extraordinary. Grand living spaces flow effortlessly between sun-soaked terraces, resort-style entertaining zones, and serene private retreats—each moment framed by the ever-changing harbour panorama.\r\n\r\nThe residence features five indulgent bedrooms and eight luxurious bathrooms, including a master suite that redefines elegance—complete with a private terrace, panoramic views, and a spa-inspired ensuite sanctuary.\r\n\r\nFrom the rooftop bar and panoramic viewing decks to the cinema, wine and whisky cellar, and private office, this home is designed for both celebration and seclusion. An internal lift glides between the top three levels, while a self-contained guest suite on the lower level offers the ideal space for guests, extended family, or staff—all with absolute privacy.\r\n\r\nOutdoors, manicured grounds include a tranquil water feature, putting green, and a private path leading directly to Tamaki Drive—a privilege unique to this address.\r\n\r\nFor the enthusiast or collector, the six-car garaging (including a separate Tamaki Drive–level garage ideal for a Sealegs or classic car) offers exceptional convenience and security.\r\n\r\nPerfectly positioned moments from St Heliers Bay’s vibrant cafés, beaches, and premier schools, this residence is more than a home—it is a statement of prestige, privacy, and permanence.\r\n\r\nOpportunities of this calibre are exceptionally rare—and once gone, may never come again. This is more than a home. It’s a legacy.\r\n\r\nPrivate viewings by appointment only.\r\n\r\nPlease contact: Brendan Goodwin on 021 278 7770 or email brendan@uniq.nz\r\n\r\nPLEASE NOTE: The technical information provided (including floor plan and section sizes, for example) has been sourced from third-party organisations such as Cotality, LINZ, and Auckland Council. It is provided as a broad guide for general information only. It is intended to provide a general understanding of the subject matter.",
